, {"label": "deezer", "url": "https://www.deezer.com/search/kynlary", "search": true}, {"label": "discogs", "url": "https://www.discogs.com/search/?q=kynlary&type=all", "search": true}], "notes": ["“a couple tracks back we had some stuff from this Plug artist that played on the show a bit before, King Larry”", "mentioned by the presenter but we couldn't work out when it played", "Kynlary (Trevion Lamonta Brown, Atlanta) is a real plugg-scene rapper/producer linked to the #Twilight collective — 'King Larry' is a plausible ASR mishearing of his name; specific track not identified."]}, {"t": null, "time": "--:--:--", "artist": "Z3ak", "title": null, "conf": "low", "links": [{"label": "bandcamp", "url": "https://bandcamp.com/search?q=Z3ak", "search": true}, {"label": "youtube", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Z3ak", "search": true}, {"label": "soundcloud", "url": "https://soundcloud.com/search?q=Z3ak", "search": true}, {"label": "spotify", "url": "https://open.spotify.com/search/Z3ak", "search": true}, {"label": "apple", "url": "https://music.apple.com/au/search?term=Z3ak", "search": true}, {"label": "deezer", "url": "https://www.deezer.com/search/Z3ak", "search": true}, {"label": "discogs", "url": "https://www.discogs.com/search/?q=Z3ak&type=all", "search": true}], "notes": ["“just before we heard Zeke Z-E-3-A-K we've heard a few songs from him over the past weeks”", "mentioned by the presenter but we couldn't work out when it played"]}], "counts": {"high": 3, "mid": 7, "low": 19}, "transcripts": [{"start": "00:02:17", "end": "00:05:08", "text": "FBi Radio 94.5 FM. You're listening to Right Click New TAB. My name's Lindsay. I'm with you till three this morning. Thanks to Marcus for the last couple hours on Sleepless with Sydney. Broadcasting from the FBi Radio studios, Gadigal land, Redfin, Alexandra. Always was, always will be. FBI is really lucky to have been in this space for 20-ish odd years but Gadigal people have owned this land for generations before and that's an ownership that will continue well beyond us here. If you don't know about FBI, a community radio station, independent, not-for-profit has been its entire run. Everyone that does radio does so as a volunteer and we do it for the passion of sharing amazing, fun, music, talks, culture. encounters from our city. We're in the middle of our supporter drive at the moment. It's with support from listeners like yourself that we get to keep doing what we do here on the radio. So if you're in the position to help us out here at FBI, that ongoing support is just essential to just keep the place ticking along day after day. FBI.radio slash support is the place to go to do that. This show, right click new tab, is focused on looking at music from the present music of the present unpacking it looking at it from different angles seeing what crazy music people are making at the moment and why i feel like this episode is gonna this broadcast is gonna go in some wild directions um looking at new music as a very expansive in a very from a very expansive position We started off by a collaboration by two incredible Kenyan artists, Slickback and Kamuru, from a collab AB from a while ago. This song is a band from a while ago. They're called Sleeper and Snake. This song, Baptized, I believe this is like the first official release from it. It's from a local label, record store, Prop Records, a new compilation they've put out recently. this kind of I guess yeah questions about interesting questions about new music something maybe recorded a while ago but shared with us now 0434 0435123945 is the text line number I'd love to hear from you and let's chat soon you're on FBI radio"}, {"start": "00:13:43", "end": "00:14:22", "text": "Listening to Right Click New Tab, listening to Philly band Trusselina. Heard them on the show before, this is a track off their debut record, The Point, I Trust, My Trusselina, The Club. Kind of that Philly DIY scene, tag about adjacent bands. This song's called The Club. Kind of leaning into more the bedroom pop side of things. We also heard a brand new thing from Keanu Nelson and a track by Killer featuring a bunch of the sort of DMV ambient rap."}, {"start": "00:14:27", "end": "00:14:58", "text": "I love listening to weird and wonderful new music on this show, and I think we might do that for the next little bit. Um, some fun glitchy SoundCloud stuff. You're in FBi. Yeah. Fuck."}, {"start": "00:15:10", "end": "00:15:38", "text": "Yeah, yeah, yeah. Listen. Got an account manager. Playful banter with the clerk. Yeah. Put a bag on a shirt. Fuck it. Walk inside a club, made a jump. Very few is really fucking there from the jump. But you know I see ya. But you know I see ya. Y'all know I see ya."}, {"start": "00:30:44", "end": "00:31:04", "text": "Okay so I'm walking home from the grocery store, right? Okay so I'm walking home from the grocery store, right? When all of this funk is... O funk é um dos ritmos mais difíceis de fazer e eu vou te provar o porquê. Sabazon. Olha a ideia do...da questão. Yeah."}, {"start": "00:32:24", "end": "00:33:21", "text": "Yeah, look, it's... Right-click New TAB on FBi Radio. Take a very radical approach to new music on this show. And, yeah, enjoyed that last little stretch of, I think, a delve into a lot of different current sounds in the hip-hop rap sphere on SoundCloud. um some of the really wild fx spam slash um oh my god the other name for it has just completely slipped my mind but i did say it before um jug um yeah this offshoot of jerk music um allow you like your xavier so based sort of sound that's just spiraled into just like totally unhinged and totally experimental forms of"}, {"start": "00:33:32", "end": "00:35:09", "text": "and Fidelity to just like all sorts of crazy extremes and then a bit of like um yeah glitchy stuff from artists like um uh Zayok we just heard Gunk with most of them we've heard in the show in the past and a couple of other artists I'll have the track list up probably after the show just because we're burning through tracks so quickly at the moment um for you to grab them all but yeah some some glitchy stuff that also kind of stepped into that step team world um yeah all these sort of sounds which are just like cross-pollinating it like the craziest fear it's just hard to even catch up and and um and categorize them but i think that's what's so exciting about it as well right now we're listening to dj leucinius another favorite of the show known for his Wayne, I would say, known for his Barley Funk stuff, but also for these sort of, like, medley slash mash-up mini songs that he cranks out. But he's been a bit on a bit of a, as we can hear now, like, he's been a bit on, like, a bit of a footwork vibe recently, which is cool. So we're gonna listen to a couple of those. Recharge, and we'll see where we go from here. Reminder, it's FBI Radio Support Drive at the moment. FBI.radio.com is the place to go to be a part of that. Here on Backlink Viewtab."}, {"start": "00:35:51", "end": "00:36:10", "text": "O homem não tem esse tipo de problema, o homem macho não dá insônia, insônia é doença de fresco, bota a cabeça no travesseiro, fecha os olhos que você vai dormir, só isso. Eu fui colocar a gasolina aqui na moto, aí quando eu abri o tanque, meu fone de ouvido caiu aqui dentro. Aí quando eu ligo a moto, olha só o barulho que sai do cana."}, {"start": "00:39:58", "end": "00:40:14", "text": "Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah."}, {"start": "00:49:24", "end": "00:49:50", "text": "Definitely more IDM-y than the previous stuff we heard from her, which, yeah, I guess the more recent stuff, a bit more bass-y. But yeah, still, still some kick to this. The next couple stuff is off a new EP by 3.3 E.M.Y.B.W. The first one's a remix by Side Project, and then the second in original."}, {"start": "01:10:47", "end": "01:12:00", "text": "forms pushing pushing it to the extreme and yeah like FBi such a great place to find your music I'm sure if you're listening through fbi.radio slash support wouldn't you like to support a drive at the moment uh only a few days left so help us keep ticking along for an independent non-for-profit community radio station uh help me keep playing freaky awesome music for you here for another hour 0435123945 is the text line number if uh if you want to get in touch thanks to trina for texting in trina you sound awfully familiar to an old texter from way back in my day and i'm wondering if it's you but i won't dox you uh he had an old name back then but also five letters if i'm mistaken my apologies you're on by clicking your tab on fbi radio"}, {"start": "01:19:25", "end": "01:19:50", "text": "Following in the lineage of, I guess, following in the trail of SoundCloud editing stuff, it's an artist Sean Potter, kind of like Ben Bino DJ adjacent. I think we listened to them before in the show, but this is a secondary account which I only discovered today."}, {"start": "01:19:56", "end": "01:20:52", "text": "Um, hidden burner accounts, and then here like this, uh, interesting approaches to song formats where this is a, this is called Mediterranean Boy, mix number 081364, so we've got, um, I don't know, I would call it a track disguised as a mix, because it's only five minutes long, I don't know if the mix could be five minutes long. but yeah SoundCloud Burner accounts are always fun that sort of stuff there's not one more after this but I think it's just one idea instead of like the seven that are in here and then maybe a couple more edsy stuff otherwise we might go to some more fun rap stuff you might click a new tab on FBI"}, {"start": "01:33:16", "end": "01:33:41", "text": "Right click new tab on FBi, we indulge in a bit of Soundcloud edit. Fairy dust. A couple of the more popular ones, uno dos, la cumbia, or popular accounts. If you say artists, sometimes feels like not the right word to use because who knows if they're collectives or people or whatever."}, {"start": "01:33:49", "end": "01:34:20", "text": "Unurrus Ex La Cumbia I feel like following in the vein of like Jutsu Mimani Kudori edit stuff but has like a bit I think this one like very like SoundCloudian mannerism. And before this a new track by Scan Skyboss and this is this and the song after this couple songs by producer One of One."}, {"start": "01:41:05", "end": "01:41:22", "text": "I told you I'm sorry, I didn't have time, I got lost in a party. I put up in Chevy next year, I'm a B and a two-seat Raleigh. My car wasn't starting, still took you on dates and I paid for it hardly. I didn't have nothing, it's still found no..."}, {"start": "01:42:16", "end": "01:42:33", "text": "I told you I'm sorry, I didn't have time, I got lost in a party. I put up in Chevy next year, I'm gonna be in a two-seat Raleigh. My car wasn't starting, still took you on dates and I paid for it hardly. I didn't have nothing, it's still fun."}, {"start": "01:43:15", "end": "01:43:42", "text": "Right click new tab, a couple tracks back we had some stuff from this Plug artist that played on the show a bit before, King Larry, really really like this stuff, keeping the flickering flame of Plug alive on SoundCloud but I feel like with some of their recent releases, including those two we heard, yeah so we got that super like wailing and emotional auto-tuning Plug and B vocals."}, {"start": "01:43:51", "end": "01:44:21", "text": "like aggressive fried kick drum and the second one like the way it glitches all over the place very reminiscent of some of the stuff we heard earlier in the show the jockey stuff um yeah that was the song that wasn't that's on your radio intention of glitching um and just before we heard Zeke Z-E-3-A-K we've heard a few songs from him over the past weeks on one of those really exciting ones where every song he puts out is"}, {"start": "01:44:30", "end": "01:45:36", "text": "I thought maybe we'd end on a bit of a party note, I don't know. Yeah, lots of new music for this show. Thi